    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48741" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">transactĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		transigo (postclass.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A completing</i>, <i>completion</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mundi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 55 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ennod. Ep. 1, 6</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			jurid. Lat., <i>an agreement</i>, <i>transaction</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">de transactionibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
				2</span></i>
			, tit. 15; 50, 16, 230.</div>
